WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.013
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.313 --> 00:00:08.874
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:16.064
Unit eighteen: Entrepreneurship Basics. Today you will talk about real future possibilities with the first conditional.

4
00:00:16.364 --> 00:00:19.121
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:23.218
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:25.166
Entrepreneur.

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.160
Entrepreneur means a person who starts a business.

8
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.109
My aunt is an entrepreneur with a bakery.

9
00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:35.288
Your turn. Say: Entrepreneur.

10
00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.355
Entrepreneur.

11
00:00:40.117 --> 00:00:41.362
Business idea.

12
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:45.081
Business idea means a plan for something to sell.

13
00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:47.927
Her business idea is a bike repair app.

14
00:00:48.517 --> 00:00:51.633
Your turn. Say: Business idea.

15
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.884
Business idea.

16
00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.419
Risk.

17
00:00:58.417 --> 00:01:01.136
Risk means the chance that something bad may happen.

18
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.680
Every business has some risk.

19
00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:06.854
Your turn. Say: Risk.

20
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.782
Risk.

21
00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:12.564
Investment.

22
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.699
Investment means money you put in to make more money.

23
00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:19.341
The shop needs a small investment.

24
00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.010
Your turn. Say: Investment.

25
00:01:24.867 --> 00:01:25.879
Investment.

26
00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:27.478
Market.

27
00:01:28.483 --> 00:01:31.017
Market means the people who might buy something.

28
00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:33.999
Students are a big market for snacks.

29
00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:37.294
Your turn. Say: Market.

30
00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.018
Market.

31
00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:42.726
Startup.

32
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:45.937
Startup means a new, small company.

33
00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.944
The startup makes eco-friendly bags.

34
00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.947
Your turn. Say: Startup.

35
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:55.789
Startup.

36
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.389
Profit.

37
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:01.079
Profit means money you keep after paying costs.

38
00:02:01.683 --> 00:02:03.869
We made a profit of fifty dollars.

39
00:02:04.483 --> 00:02:07.008
Your turn. Say: Profit.

40
00:02:09.867 --> 00:02:10.728
Profit.

41
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:12.566
Innovation.

42
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.084
Innovation means a new idea or method.

43
00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:19.008
Innovation helps small businesses grow.

44
00:02:19.617 --> 00:02:22.165
Your turn. Say: Innovation.

45
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:25.989
Innovation.

46
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:30.253
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.534
Visal, would you like to be an entrepreneur?

48
00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:39.021
Yes! If you take a smart risk, your startup might succeed.

49
00:02:40.117 --> 00:02:41.791
What is your business idea?

50
00:02:42.883 --> 00:02:48.519
Healthy snacks for students. If we sell them at school, we will reach a big market.

51
00:02:49.617 --> 00:02:50.711
What about money?

52
00:02:51.817 --> 00:02:56.719
If I save for six months, I will have enough for a small investment.

53
00:02:57.867 --> 00:02:59.622
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:00.483 --> 00:03:03.098
Grammar focus: First conditional.

55
00:03:03.398 --> 00:03:04.585
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:05.283 --> 00:03:08.397
If you take a smart risk, your startup might succeed.

57
00:03:09.283 --> 00:03:12.409
If we sell online, we will reach more customers.

58
00:03:13.317 --> 00:03:16.106
If the price is too high, people won't buy it.

59
00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:21.344
Use the present simple after 'if', not 'will'. Use 'might' when you are less sure.

60
00:03:22.083 --> 00:03:26.756
Be careful! Don't say: If you will take a smart risk, you might succeed.

61
00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.594
Say: If you take a smart risk, you might succeed.

62
00:03:31.894 --> 00:03:34.926
Use the present simple after 'if' in the first conditional.

63
00:03:35.733 --> 00:03:38.769
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:40.754
Starting Small.

65
00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:44.319
An entrepreneur turns a business idea into a startup.

66
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:47.066
First, they study the market.

67
00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:51.459
If the idea solves a real problem, people will buy it.

68
00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:55.209
Every startup has risk and needs some investment.

69
00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.709
If you keep improving with innovation, you will make a profit.

70
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.022
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.883 --> 00:04:08.858
If you blank a smart risk, you might succeed.

72
00:04:09.158 --> 00:04:12.150
A, take. B, will take. C, took.

73
00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.641
The answer is A: take.

74
00:04:18.783 --> 00:04:21.294
Money you keep after paying costs is blank.

75
00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.957
A, profit. B, risk. C, market.

76
00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.209
The answer is A: profit.

77
00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.547
A new, small company is a blank.

78
00:04:33.847 --> 00:04:37.744
A, startup. B, market. C, profit.

79
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.195
The answer is A: startup.

80
00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.598
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.169
What business idea would you like to start someday?

82
00:04:59.983 --> 00:05:01.542
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:01.842 --> 00:05:10.810
I would like to start a small café that uses local produce. If I work hard and save money, I will open it after university.

84
00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.703
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:13.617 --> 00:05:17.372
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and first conditional.

86
00:05:17.672 --> 00:05:22.600
Today's value is innovation. Try new ideas boldly, and learn from every attempt.

87
00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.912
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

88
00:05:26.212 --> 00:05:29.329
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

